WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.699
Film Courage: Your book The Hollywood Game
Plan…so you’ve written a lot of things

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:08.400
about how people can get their foot in the
door, thank you notes and other useful information.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.920
I want to talk about the over 40 population
and their approach.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.230
Maybe they are new to the industry, here (in
Hollywood) from somewhere else or another

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.770
line of work.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.560
Do those same rules apply?

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.760
What is working for a person over 40?

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.670
What is working against them and how do they
combat what’s not working?

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.890
Carole Kirschner: That’s a good question.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.839
Ageism totally exists in this business.

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:36.539
To say it doesn’t would be to say a lie.

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:41.550
However, the way you can protect yourself
against it is with your material.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.289
There are two things.

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:48.500
One is having great material that is undeniable.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.140
People don’t care if it’s (again I’m
thinking about screenwriters let’s say)

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.179
on the page, it doesn’t matter.

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:00.449
The other thing is to stay contemporary.

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:08.130
If you don’t know what Reddit is or what
LinkedIn or (I can’t imagine anybody who

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:14.920
doesn’t know what Twitter is) but if you
don’t know what is happening then that ages

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:15.920
you.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.710
I’ve told a lot of writers who are over
40, make a web series.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:31.780
Show that you know what is going on and it’s
a way to make you undeniable.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.460
Ageism is there but there’s a lot of people
who say “We’re looking for somebody who

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.780
has some life experience.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:44.260
I’m not looking for somebody who just got
out of USC, who made three student films,

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:51.570
has had no life and has only consumed entertainment
and doesn’t have any life experience.”

00:01:51.570 --> 00:02:00.570
So I think that the only person that is going
to get in the way is you if you’re thinking

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.939
“I’m too old.”

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:06.979
If your material is there, if you’re contemporary
with what’s going on in the business and

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:12.350
trends in society, I don’t think it’s
going to be a problem.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:18.520
Film Courage: So then look at the [news] headlines,
research what companies are doing well, what

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:25.800
is the latest social media app…like for
me with SnapChat I’m still learning about

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.800
it.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.940
I don’t really know how to use it and I
feel like that dates me because so many people

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.500
that are under 25, they’re all about SnapChat.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.580
And so there’s a demographic, there’s
a population that I don’t know about, I

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.040
don’t know how to work it and all the things
that are a part of it.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:45.280
Let’s say someone wants to get an entry
level (a mailroom) position or an administrative

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.590
assistant or receptionist, being 40?

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:48.900
Carole Kirschner: It’s harder.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.030
It’s going to be tougher.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:58.780
I know one guy who was a lawyer but all he
wanted to do was be a writer and he ended

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:05.400
up getting a job as the assistant to the Showrunner
on SVU.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.910
He did that for two years.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.590
He was the most overqualified assistant that
ever existed!

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:16.290
And then he got a job as a staff writer and
he was in his 40’s.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.230
It is very hard to get an entry-level job.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:26.260
What I recommend that people do…somebody
just emailed me and said “What can I do?

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.010
I want to be an executive.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.380
I’m 48.”

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.900
And I said “Be a producer first.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.560
Have a body of work under your belt.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.760
Come in with material.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.380
Come in showing that you can produce work.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:47.480
But I think it’s really hard unless you’ve
been a professional administrative assistant

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.850
to get a job as an administrative 
assistant when you’re over 40.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:56.470
It’s not impossible because some people
don’t care but it’s more challenging.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:57.930
It’s definitely more challenging.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:03.210
Film Courage: Well not to advocate lying on
a resume, but do you leave off…let’s suppose

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.960
I have so much work experience to show them
[in my head I’m thinking] they are definitely

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.680
going to want to hire me, maybe that works
against you?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.340
Carole Kirschner: It does work against you!

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.020
Don’t go back more than 10 years.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:17.790
I definitely tell my clients, they don’t
need to see anything from 2002.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.220
Absolutely not!

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:23.650
And what I also tell my clients is tell me
how old you really are and then if they are

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.530
over a certain age I say “Don’t tell anybody
else.”

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.410
Film Courage: Interesting.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.740
Even if you get to know co-workers?

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.160
Carole Kirschner: If you get to know co-workers
and you’re close, you can.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.600
But actually I’d keep it pretty close to
the vest.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.430
Film Courage: Interesting.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.840
I’ve known people for years.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.930
I have no idea what their ages are and I never
ask.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.970
But then some people are much more free with
information.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.040
Do you think being free with it hurts you?

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:51.540
Carole Kirschner: I wouldn’t be free with
it.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:57.780
If you are older than most of the people you’re
working with, I wouldn’t sling that around.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.770
I just wouldn’t make a deal of it.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.340
Film Courage: Right…okay.

